<article class="env-lemma" id="0FMM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FMM">Lemma <span data-tag="0FMM">50.12.1</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a quasi-compact, quasi-separated, and smooth morphism of schemes over a base scheme $S$. There is a bounded spectral sequence with first page </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  E_1^{p, q} = H^ q(\Omega ^ p_{Y/S} \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ Y}^\mathbf {L} Rf_*\Omega ^\bullet _{X/Y})  \]
</div>
  <p> converging to $R^{p + q}f_*\Omega ^\bullet _{X/S}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Consider $\Omega ^\bullet _{X/S}$ as a filtered complex with the filtration introduced above. The spectral sequence is the spectral sequence of Cohomology, Lemma <a href="/tag/0FLL" data-tag="0FLL">20.29.5</a>. By Derived Categories of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/0FML" data-tag="0FML">36.23.2</a> we have 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  Rf_*\text{gr}^ k\Omega ^\bullet _{X/S} = \Omega ^ k_{Y/S}[-k] \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ Y}^\mathbf {L} Rf_*\Omega ^\bullet _{X/Y}  \]
</div>
    <p>
       and thus we conclude. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>